# React component file structure

**Always follow** when creating or editing `.tsx` / `.jsx` files. Full reference: `.agents/skills/react-component-sections/SKILL.md`.

## File layout

1. Imports
2. `TYPE DEFINITIONS` banner — all types/interfaces for the file
3. `COMPONENT START` banner — component implementation (`export const Name: Name = ...`)

Never put types after the component. Never interleave types and implementation.

Banner format:

```tsx
/**********************************************************************************************************
 *   TYPE DEFINITIONS
 **********************************************************************************************************/
```

```tsx
/**********************************************************************************************************
 *   COMPONENT START
 **********************************************************************************************************/
```

## Inline sections (inside the component body)

Use `/***** section *****/` comments. Include a section only when it has code; keep this order when present:

| Order | Section            |
| ----- | ------------------ |
| 1     | `state`            |
| 2     | `context`          |
| 3     | `hooks`            |
| 4     | `queries`          |
| 5     | `form`             |
| 6     | `effects`          |
| 7     | `functions`        |
| 8     | `render helpers`   |
| 9     | `render`           |

Component shape: `type Name = React.FC<{...}>` in TYPE DEFINITIONS; `export const Name: Name = ...` in COMPONENT START. **One component per file** (see `.cursor/rules/one-component-per-file.mdc`). Route and prop-less exceptions: `.agents/skills/react-component-format/SKILL.md`.
